    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 230\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 1864, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the social services law, in relation to posting\n      child day care provider qualifications on the office  of  children\n      and family services' website\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill would authorize child care providers licensed by the Office\nof Children and Family Services (OCFS) to provide the agency with infor-\nmation regarding  any  trainings  or  professional  development  courses\ncompleted  by  their  staff.  OCFS  would  then be required to make this\ninformation publicly available on its website.\n\n  I strongly encourage child care  professionals  to  take  courses  and\ntrainings  that enhance and strengthen their skills. While I support the\nintent of the bill, it  raises  significant  concerns  that  potentially\nplace children at risk. First, it would give providers complete latitude\nto  self-report  any  \"relevant training,\" without any qualifications or\nrestrictions on what  constitutes  \"training.\"  Second,  OCFS  would  be\nrequired  to accept this information and post it \"as is\" on its website.\nYet OCFS has no ability to verify the source or content of the  training\n-- let alone whether it was even completed -- thus making it widely open\nto fraud and abuse. As parents and caregivers will rely upon this infor-\nmation  when  making child care decisions, I am therefore constrained to\nveto this bill.\n\n  However, in furtherance of the shared goal of providing  parents  with\nmore  information  about  available  child care programs, I am directing\nOCFS to develop a list of enhanced trainings  that  are  verifiable  and\nrelevant  to  providing  high quality and safe child care programs. Once\ndeveloped, the list will be posted on OCFS's website. If a  licensed  or\nregistered child care provider submits adequate proof that he or she has\ncompleted one of the trainings on the approved OCFS list, then OCFS will\npost that information on its website.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 230,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2016
   }
